.TH CSTRING_TO_UPPER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_to_upper \- convert all characters to uppercase in-place
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

void cstring_to_upper(cstr s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Applies toupper() to every character of the string in place.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   String to change
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function changes only the ASCII characters reliably: for a
non-ASCII byte, the behaviour of toupper() depends on the current
locale
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_to_lower (3)
